WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
Melt a sodium salt and pass
electricity through it,

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.970
and shiny sodium metal forms
at the negative electrode.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.870
Now dissolve a sodium salt
in water, and try again.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.770
This time, bubbles of hydrogen
gas appear at that electrode.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.070
Never sodium.

6
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.530
Same metal, same electricity.

7
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.450
So why does adding water
change the product?

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.990
In this mission, you'll find out
why the ions in an electrolyte

9
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.490
must be free to move.

10
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.570
You'll see what happens at
the cathode and at the anode,

11
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.530
and learn the rules that predict
the products when a solution

12
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.730
is split by electricity.

13
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.450
Your mission: explain why
water changes what forms at the

14
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.540
cathode.
